Q: What is the good format for temperature in SwiftUI TextField? A: <p>you can use this code snipt it work for current projcet</p>
<pre><code>import Foundation

enum TemperatureFormatter {
    static func format(_ fahrenheit: Double) -&gt; String {
        let celsius = (fahrenheit - 32) * 5 / 9
        let rounded = celsius.rounded()
        let measurement = Measurement(value: rounded, unit: UnitTemperature.celsius)
        return measurement.formatted(.measurement(width: .abbreviated, usage: .weather))
    }
}

extension Double {
    func formattedTemperature() -&gt; String {
        return TemperatureFormatter.format(self)
    }
}
</code></pre>
<p>to maket it work you need to go to device/ simulator</p>
<p>General -&gt; laguage and reegin -&gt;  temperature<br />
and select one F or C</p>

Q: Is the practice of returning a C++ reference variable evil? A: <pre><code>int&amp; fun()  
{  
  int y = 10;  
  return y;  
}  
</code></pre>
<p>in the above code returning reference could lead to dangling reference problem. It depends on the situation when you should return by reference.</p>
<pre><code>int&amp; operator\[\](const int&amp; index)  
